    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "24d7d9fe_f4d02cb5",
        "filename": "driver/led/lm3630a.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1165921
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-22T17:50:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IMO using this sort of type for a parameter is not a great idea. Does the compiler have to mask the value? If you use \u0027unsigned int\u0027 then it can just use a register.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "bd26a518fec20f3cff5700704d3669d6a1f5d17a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ea2aed72_718fa413",
        "filename": "driver/led/lm3630a.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1192536
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-22T21:02:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "i2c_write8 wants to put the value into a uint8_t later, so I used that here in the hopes that the compiler would warn about incorrect uses.  Is the compiler not able to pass a uint8 in a register?  Since these are inlined, does it actually matter other than fixing the allowed range?",
      "parentUuid": "24d7d9fe_f4d02cb5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "bd26a518fec20f3cff5700704d3669d6a1f5d17a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8d3ba342_a551a720",
        "filename": "driver/led/lm3630a.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1165921
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-22T21:14:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The compiler can only use the machine registers, which in this case are 32-bit. So the only way it can enforce this is to mask off the top 24 bits.\n\nSo long as this does not actually do this, and affect code size (as you say below), I don\u0027t think it matters.",
      "parentUuid": "ea2aed72_718fa413",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "bd26a518fec20f3cff5700704d3669d6a1f5d17a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d05bdfd0_490a914e",
        "filename": "driver/led/lm3630a.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 1165921
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-22T17:50:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why make these inline? How does it affect code size?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 19,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "bd26a518fec20f3cff5700704d3669d6a1f5d17a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "44871395_cdbb656e",
        "filename": "driver/led/lm3630a.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 1192536
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-01-22T21:02:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That seems to be the convention for these helper functions in other drivers.  It makes a difference of 0 bytes in the output object (perhaps the compiler is inlining without the keyword anyway, since they\u0027re so simple and the uses are all in the same file?).  I did update to mark them as static, since they\u0027re not supposed to be exported.",
      "parentUuid": "d05bdfd0_490a914e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 19,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "bd26a518fec20f3cff5700704d3669d6a1f5d17a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
